# Line endings are not cosmetic here.
#
# With core.autocrlf=true, a Windows checkout rewrites every text file to CRLF
# in the working tree. image/ is then COPYed into an Alpine image, where a
# script starting "#!/bin/sh\r" fails with "not found" -- naming the
# interpreter, not the carriage return, so it reads as a missing shell rather
# than as a line-ending problem. The same applies to anything the container
# parses: sshd_config, sudoers, the entrypoint.
#
# Forcing LF in the working tree costs nothing on Windows -- every editor and
# toolchain in use here reads LF -- and removes the failure entirely.

* text=auto eol=lf

# PowerShell is the one place CRLF is the local convention. Harmless either
# way, since it never enters a container.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Never touched, whatever they contain.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gz  binary
*.zip binary
